# Inputs excluded from the expo-updates fingerprint (runtimeVersion policy).
#
# Opening/building this project in Android Studio makes Gradle's Buildship plugin
# write Eclipse IDE metadata INSIDE node_modules — .classpath, .project and
# .settings/ in autolinked packages (sometimes under android/, sometimes at the
# package root, e.g. expo-module-gradle-plugin). They are not in the npm tarballs,
# so EAS's clean install never has them. The local fingerprint then stops matching
# the one EAS computes, and that FAILS the build outright:
#   "Runtime version calculated on local machine ... does not match EAS"
#
# @expo/fingerprint already ignores build/, .gradle/ and .cxx/ by default — this
# IDE metadata is the gap. It is never source, so ignoring it cannot mask a real
# native change.
#
# Keep this file tracked: EAS reads it too, and both sides must ignore the same
# paths or the hashes diverge again.
**/.classpath
**/.project
**/.settings/**/*
